---
name: Send OCSF as Splunk CIM
description: |
  Map OCSF events to Splunk CIM and send them to a Splunk HTTP Event
  Collector. The CIM record becomes the HEC event, while the OCSF event next
  to it supplies the HEC metadata, such as the time and the reporting host.
---

subscribe "ocsf"
this = {ocsf: this}
splunk::cim::from_ocsf ocsf, into=cim
// The HEC metadata is not part of the CIM record. Bind it explicitly, and
// choose a source type that your Splunk deployment configures for this data.
to_splunk "https://localhost:8088",
  hec_token=secret("SPLUNK_HEC_TOKEN"),
  event=cim,
  host=ocsf.device?.hostname?,
  source=ocsf.metadata.log_name?,
  sourcetype="_json",
  index="main",
  time=ocsf.time
